  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Lesion method: subtract a region', note: 'Brain damage as a natural experiment — what the patient loses is what the region did. Broca (speech production), Wernicke (comprehension), H.M. (memory formation): the map was built by injury.' },
    { math: '2 · Double dissociations: the gold standard', note: 'Patient 1: can speak, can\'t understand. Patient 2: can understand, can\'t speak. Two independent single losses prove two separate systems — the logic that separates cognitive modules.' },
    { math: '3 · Famous syndromes as windows', note: 'Prosopagnosia (face blindness — recognition without familiarity), neglect (ignoring half of space after right parietal damage), blindsight (responding to unseen stimuli — subcortical vision), Capgras (believing family are impostors — recognition without emotional tagging).' },
    { math: '4 · Plasticity and rehabilitation', note: 'The adult brain rewires: constraint-induced therapy forces use of a paralysed limb and expands its cortical map; strokes recover through reorganisation, not regeneration. Rehabilitation is applied plasticity.' },
